 =-49 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm 7\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  $\\lambda =\\pm 7\\text{i}$ are the (purely imaginary) roots of the auxiliary equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f015153f-8a9c-578d-9435-4dc22d6628c9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f015153f-8a9c-578d-9435-4dc22d6628c9" :answer-field/id #uuid "f015153f-8a9c-578d-9435-4dc22d6628c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-622d3756-d700-5d84-8d8b-60c8973afaed" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3e1e64c8-d790-53a7-bc7e-bbf555d4681b" "answer-60a91155-f0af-53ce-9e9e-3353b022d470" "answer-1513401a-e1ba-5664-b3cf-95e373800e1e" "answer-3c8c3852-79f6-52a8-bf76-04d14a086970" "answer-622d3756-d700-5d84-8d8b-60c8973afaed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e1e64c8-d790-53a7-bc7e-bbf555d4681b" :answer/id #uuid "3e1e64c8-d790-53a7-bc7e-bbf555d4681b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\pm 7\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60a91155-f0af-53ce-9e9e-3353b022d470" :answer/id #uuid "60a91155-f0af-53ce-9e9e-3353b022d470" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7\\pm \\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1513401a-e1ba-5664-b3cf-95e373800e1e" :answer/id #uuid "1513401a-e1ba-5664-b3cf-95e373800e1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\pm 14\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c8c3852-79f6-52a8-bf76-04d14a086970" :answer/id #uuid "3c8c3852-79f6-52a8-bf76-04d14a086970" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 14\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-622d3756-d700-5d84-8d8b-60c8973afaed" :answer/id #uuid "622d3756-d700-5d84-8d8b-60c8973afaed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 7\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-036dcc56-656f-5be3-b389-bcb0f4704c57" :question/id #uuid "036dcc56-656f-5be3-b389-bcb0f4704c57" :question/math-academy-id "q-130165" :question/problem "Consider the equation ${y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+6y=0,$ where $y=y(x).$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ is a solution, then $\\lambda =$" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-4\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+6{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +6) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +6=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +6 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4)-4+6 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2}+2 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2} & =-2 \\\\ \\lambda -2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =2\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  $\\lambda =2\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}$ are the complex roots of the auxiliary equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fe8f1d1e-565e-5be4-91dc-30880a0e6067"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fe8f1d1e-565e-5be4-91dc-30880a0e6067" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe8f1d1e-565e-5be4-91dc-30880a0e6067" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-03245522-0fe0-529f-b451-6abe8b80f779" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c972df8a-ed3b-5895-a3ef-2a61194b7a3c" "answer-b3ef9807-00e5-5ea2-a26c-7dfdf73f111b" "answer-03245522-0fe0-529f-b451-6abe8b80f779" "answer-769edc59-752e-5e12-8330-8391cd08a5e2" "answer-579b2912-410b-55c0-b52c-737d3298d055"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c972df8a-ed3b-5895-a3ef-2a61194b7a3c" :answer/id #uuid "c972df8a-ed3b-5895-a3ef-2a61194b7a3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3ef9807-00e5-5ea2-a26c-7dfdf73f111b" :answer/id #uuid "b3ef9807-00e5-5ea2-a26c-7dfdf73f111b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}\\pm -2\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03245522-0fe0-529f-b451-6abe8b80f779" :answer/id #uuid "03245522-0fe0-529f-b451-6abe8b80f779" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-769edc59-752e-5e12-8330-8391cd08a5e2" :answer/id #uuid "769edc59-752e-5e12-8330-8391cd08a5e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-579b2912-410b-55c0-b52c-737d3298d055" :answer/id #uuid "579b2912-410b-55c0-b52c-737d3298d055" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\pm \\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5ec1eb1a-35a3-5483-b0fc-d5a9a680836b" :question/id #uuid "5ec1eb1a-35a3-5483-b0fc-d5a9a680836b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130171" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+3{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +3=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +3 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +1)-1+3 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2}+2 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2} & =-2 \\\\ \\lambda +1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-1\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2}x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2}x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dcd58d31-460d-5db3-9cc3-21dda899bae5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dcd58d31-460d-5db3-9cc3-21dda899bae5" :answer-field/id #uuid "dcd58d31-460d-5db3-9cc3-21dda899bae5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b774558a-559a-5988-8403-8737cd918d6c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-372decf5-07c1-53da-bc75-d9a5d1ca2af2" "answer-f3b188bb-b260-50c5-829b-55f980ff4f25" "answer-81bc7a0f-e18c-5f02-830e-17220310bc9f" "answer-b774558a-559a-5988-8403-8737cd918d6c" "answer-5aca1eff-3ec7-558c-b8b7-98e8fbd1724d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-372decf5-07c1-53da-bc75-d9a5d1ca2af2" :answer/id #uuid "372decf5-07c1-53da-bc75-d9a5d1ca2af2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-\\sqrt{2}x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3b188bb-b260-50c5-829b-55f980ff4f25" :answer/id #uuid "f3b188bb-b260-50c5-829b-55f980ff4f25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-\\sqrt{2}x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2}x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2}x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81bc7a0f-e18c-5f02-830e-17220310bc9f" :answer/id #uuid "81bc7a0f-e18c-5f02-830e-17220310bc9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b774558a-559a-5988-8403-8737cd918d6c" :answer/id #uuid "b774558a-559a-5988-8403-8737cd918d6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2}x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2}x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5aca1eff-3ec7-558c-b8b7-98e8fbd1724d" :answer/id #uuid "5aca1eff-3ec7-558c-b8b7-98e8fbd1724d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2}x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2}x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a7ffe364-7a92-504c-8ec6-763abcbb5581" :question/id #uuid "a7ffe364-7a92-504c-8ec6-763abcbb5581" :question/math-academy-id "q-130169" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+20y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+4\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+20{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +20) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +20=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +20 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4)-4+20 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2} & =-16 \\\\ \\lambda +2 & =\\pm 4\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-2\\pm 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f9a6370f-e406-5a8c-ad57-f67b9f3a356b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f9a6370f-e406-5a8c-ad57-f67b9f3a356b" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9a6370f-e406-5a8c-ad57-f67b9f3a356b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-58f5d98e-6fb6-528b-b0ee-2573b379c1a2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-58f5d98e-6fb6-528b-b0ee-2573b379c1a2" "answer-246b2565-637f-5292-abfa-d2862a24940b" "answer-f13d0b8d-e943-5792-a3b5-b8da7091ae7b" "answer-70d70171-451c-5304-897d-4e4efdb95d05" "answer-3039ea89-084f-5591-9fca-1787fe1eb56d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58f5d98e-6fb6-528b-b0ee-2573b379c1a2" :answer/id #uuid "58f5d98e-6fb6-528b-b0ee-2573b379c1a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-246b2565-637f-5292-abfa-d2862a24940b" :answer/id #uuid "246b2565-637f-5292-abfa-d2862a24940b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f13d0b8d-e943-5792-a3b5-b8da7091ae7b" :answer/id #uuid "f13d0b8d-e943-5792-a3b5-b8da7091ae7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-4x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70d70171-451c-5304-897d-4e4efdb95d05" :answer/id #uuid "70d70171-451c-5304-897d-4e4efdb95d05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-4x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3039ea89-084f-5591-9fca-1787fe1eb56d" :answer/id #uuid "3039ea89-084f-5591-9fca-1787fe1eb56d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186088864 :tutorial/content "Recall our solution from the previous slide:\n\n$$\ny = Ae^{2\\textrm{i}x} + Be^{-2\\textrm{i}x}.\n$$\n\nWe use **Euler's formula**, which states \n\n$$\ne^{\\textrm{i}\\theta} = \\cos\\theta + \\textrm{i}\\sin\\theta,\n$$\n\n to rewrite the exponentials:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+B(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) \\\\  & =(A+B)\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+\\text{i}(A-B)\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we are typically solving for a real-world quantity, our final answer must be a real-valued function. For this to be true, the arbitrary constants $A$ and $B$ must be a complex conjugate pair ($B = \\overline{A}$). This implies that the following definitions yield *real* constants $P$ and $Q$:\n\n$$\nP = A+B \\quad \\text{and} \\quad Q = \\textrm{i}(A-B).\n$$\n\nThis gives the **general real-valued solution**:\n\n$$\n\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{y(x) = P\\cos{2x} + Q\\sin{2x}},\n$$\n\nwhere $P$ and $Q$ are arbitrary real constants determined by initial conditions.\n\nSo, for example,\n\n$$\ny(x) = \\cos{2x} - 2\\sin{2x},\n$$\n\ncorresponding to $P=1$ and $Q=-2,$ is a solution of the given differential equation. On the other hand,\n\n$$\ny(x) = \\cos{2x} + \\sin{x}\n$$\n\nis *not* a solution because it contains a function $\\sin{x},$ which is not included in the above form representing the general solution." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186088957 :tutorial/content "In general, if the characteristic equation of a second-order homogeneous ODE has **imaginary roots** \n\n$$\n\\lambda = \\pm b\\textrm{i},\n$$\n\nthen the *general solution* is\n\n$$\ny(x) = Ae^{\\textrm{i} b x} + B e^{-\\textrm{i} bx}.\n$$\n\nUsing *Euler's formula*, the above can be simplified to\n\n$$\ny(x) = P \\cos bx + Q \\sin bx,\n$$\n\nwhere $P = A+B$ and $Q=\\textrm{i} (A-B).$\n\nLet's take a look at another example." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186088863 :tutorial/content "Recall that our general solution is\n\n$$\ny = Ae^{(3 + 3 \\textrm{i})x} + Be^{(3 - 3 \\textrm{i})x}.\n$$\n\nOur goal is to simplify this to find the **real-valued general solution**. We can do this using **Euler's formula**, which states that \n\n$$\ne^{\\textrm{i}\\theta} = \\cos{\\theta} + \\textrm{i}\\sin{\\theta}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we use the law of exponents to separate the real and imaginary parts in the exponential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A{e}^{3x}{e}^{3\\text{i}x}+B{e}^{3x}{e}^{-3\\text{i}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}(A{e}^{3\\text{i}x}+B{e}^{-3\\text{i}x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we apply Euler's formula with $\\theta = 3x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{3x}(A(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)+B(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)) \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}((A+B)\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\text{i}(A-B)\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants, we can define new arbitrary constants $P=A+B$ and $Q=\\textrm{i}(A-B).$ The general solution becomes:\n\n$$\n\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{y = e^{3x}(P\\cos{3 x} + Q\\sin{3 x}).}\n$$\n\nThis is the final form of the solution, written entirely with real-valued functions.\n\nSo, for example,\n\n$$\ny(x) = e^{3x}(5\\cos{3 x} - \\sin{3 x}),\n$$\n\ncorresponding to $P=5$ and $Q=-1,$ is a solution of the given differential equation. On the other hand,\n\n$$\ny(x) =  e^{3x}(\\cos{5 x} - \\sin{3 x})\n$$\n\nis *not* a solution because it contains a function $e^{3x}\\cos{5x},$ which is not included in the above form representing the general solution." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186088958 :tutorial/content "In general, if the characteristic equation of a second-order homogeneous ODE has **complex conjugate roots** \n\n$$\n\\lambda = a \\pm b\\textrm{i},\n$$\n\n then the *general solution* is\n\n$$\ny(x) = Ae^{(a+b\\textrm{i})x} + B e^{(a-b\\textrm{i})x}.\n$$\n\nUsing *Euler's formula*, we can expand and group the terms:\n\n$$\ny(x) = e^{ax} \\left[ (A+B)\\cos bx + \\textrm{i}(A-B)\\sin bx \\right].\n$$\n\nThis simplifies to\n\n$$\ny(x) = e^{ax} \\left( P \\cos bx + Q \\sin bx \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $P = A+B$ and $Q=\\textrm{i} (A-B).$\n\nLet's take a look at another example" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087945 :activity/expected-seconds 780.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
